ishes of the bene jesuit  and bore later a son paul in the dune  universe at benejesser can choose the  sex of their child it isn't until paul  is tested by the reverend mother helen  mohaym that she believes paul might be  the one that's why she goes to baron  vladimir harkenin and asks him to spare  jessica and paul when they attack  arrakis when paul ingests spice during  the spice harvester rescue he is haunted  by voices which echo the words kwitsat's  hattera  and before he fights jamas we hear this  in one of his visions  i argue this is more of a metaphorical  death paul will need to cast aside his  old name to become something new in the  novel paul takes the name wadeeb this is  derived from the small mouse of the  desert which we see in part one one of  the most cryptic parts of dune part 1  are paul's visions now i actually  extracted every vision and put them in  chronological order because i'm a crazy  person so that i could get a better  grasp of what's going on here the first  thing to note are that the visions  aren't a hundred percent accurate in  fact they can be completely wrong paul  dreams of both pajamas teaching him in  the desert and james killing him neither  of these are true the dreams are merely  several of the possible futures paul  could encounter the 1984 film confirms  the unreliability of these visions your  mother wants you to tell me about your  dreams  do they come  true not all of them  i know which ones will believe it or not  there are roughly four to five minutes  of paul's visions scattered throughout  the film appearing in most of these  visions is chaney she'll later become  paul's lover and father of his children  not seen in the 1984 version but likely  to appear in part 2 paul and cheney have  a son who is killed by beast rabban  harkonnen this might be what spurs paul  and the fremen in their final attack  against the harkonnen and the emperor we  do get this vision of paul taking on the  sardakar which could be part of the epic  battle of arakin which occurs at the end  of dune and sees paul become emperor i  love how you can even see a sandworm  fighting alongside them in this vision  it's chaney who guides him into battle  but in the 1984 version she's battling  alongside him which i think is more  likely to happen in part two as well we  also see a vision of jessica holding a  baby we know that she's pregnant with  paul's sister in the books jessica takes  the water of life while pregnant i won't  get into too much detail but the water  of life allows a bene gesserate to  ascend to reverend mother granting them  far greater powers this ascension causes  jessica to prematurely give birth and  the process gives her a daughter who  will come to be known as alia alia will  have incredible powers similar to her  brother paul and will play a pivotal  role in dune part 2. she's the one who  will actually kill baron harkin and not  mentioned in the film that baron is  actually her grandfather for those of  you who don't know jessica is the  illegitimate child of the baron which  would also make paul his grandson  perhaps most cryptic of the visions is  chaney's bloody hand and the kris knife  made from a tooth of a sandworm it's  implied here that she's the one to kill  paul this never happens in the dew novel  and i interpret this as one of two  things a a future that does not happen  or be a metaphor for the blood on paul's  hands when he begins his crusade across  the galaxy after the events of dune paul  becomes emperor but not everyone is too  excited about that he embarks on a  crusade which at the beginning of the  children of dune mini-series has already  killed 60 billion people now you might  be asking yourself i thought paul was  this nice guy fighting for justice how  is this possible well because paul can  see into the future he has to navigate  humanity in such a way that prevents its  own annihilation and part of this path  means embarking on a crusade but here we  see that young paul hates what future  paul has become i see a holy war  spreading across the universe like  unquenchable fire a warrior religion  that weighs the atreides banner in my  father's name if you want to learn more  about what happens after the events of  dune i suggest you check out both my  dune 1984 and children of dune videos  paul makes the decision to stay on dune  even after his mother suggested they be  smuggled off planet he tells the fremen  that the atreides came to dune not for  the spices or riches but for the  strength of its people desert power the  emperor sent the atreides to dune to die  so paul will stay and fight back you may  also recall that this woman kines was  tasked with getting off planet and  telling various houses of the landsrod  who would be sympathetic to the atreides  of the betrayal that occurred on arrakis  and that paul is still alive this would  undoubtedly cause a civil war within the  empire to avoid this paul throws out the  suggestion he marry one of the emperor's  daughters since the emperor has no male  heirs this would unite the two warring  factions although this is quickly  dismissed by his mother and kinds this  will become a reality later on for him  when he ascends to emperor he'll marry  princess ireland carino one of the  emperor's daughters this is a political  marriage to help keep the peace and he's  still very much in love with cheney and  the two end up having twins paul ends up  seeing a friend and warrior riding a  sand worm what kinds was trying to do  before she was cut down by the sardakar  he refers to this ability as desert  power the same thing his father wanted  to unlock on arrakis in the 84 version  of dune you'll see how paul will  eventually be able to ride worms and  control them something that will prove  worthwhile when taking on the emperor  but the last line of the film goes to  cheney who says this is only the  beginning and for paul it is this is the  beginning of his journey to become  muadib the kwitsat's hararak which part  2 will delve into as of today an imdb  page has just been made for dune part 2  which has the synopsis duke paula  tradies joins the freeman and begins a  spiritual and martial journey to become  muadeeb while trying to prevent the  horrible but inevitable future he's  witnessed a holy war in his name  spreading throughout the universe i  don't know about you guys but i  absolutely love this version of dune and  if you're looking for more content i  have three other videos from differences  between this version and 1984 as well as  ending explains for children of dune and  the 84 version so be sure to check those  out thanks for watching everyone make  sure to like and subscribe and for more  bad takes you can follow me on twitter  and instagram at thingstoryt until next  time remember daddy loves you very much
 

